<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>DQ Caramel Sundae — The Sweet, Buttery Option</h2>
<p>DQ's caramel topping is a thick, sweet, buttery sauce poured over cold soft serve. The caramel at DQ is more viscous than the hot fudge — it clings to the soft serve rather than melting into it as quickly. The result is a dessert where caramel flavor is present in every spoonful throughout the entire cup. Find all DQ classic treats on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>
<h2>Caramel vs. Hot Fudge Sundae — Which to Choose?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Caramel Sundae</strong> — Sweeter, more viscous, buttery flavor profile. Best for caramel fans and guests who prefer a lighter, non-chocolate dessert.</li>
  <li><strong>Hot Fudge Sundae</strong> — Rich chocolate, warm-cold temperature contrast. Best for chocolate fans who want the classic sundae experience.</li>
  <li>Both are $3.79. Choose based on flavor preference — chocolate or caramel. Both are excellent value at the same price.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Caramel Sundae in the DQ Value Lineup</h2>
<p>The Caramel Sundae is included as the Small Sundae option in the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a>. It is also one of the eligible choices when a sundae is included with combos or promotions. At $3.79 individually, it represents strong value — a dessert at approximately the same price as a small fries.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How much is the DQ Caramel Sundae?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">$3.79 with 310 calories.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is the Caramel Sundae available at every DQ?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes. The Caramel Sundae is available at all DQ locations — both Grill &amp; Chill and Treat locations.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can I get caramel and hot fudge on the same sundae?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes, at most locations. Ask for a combined caramel and hot fudge topping — sometimes called a Turtle Sundae. May cost slightly more than a single-topping sundae.</div></div></div></div>
<p style="margin-top:32px;">For the complete DQ menu with all categories and deals, visit <a href="/"><strong>The Queen Dairy Menu</strong></a>.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Caramel Sundae — The Richest of the Three</h2>
    <p>DQ's three sundae options are all priced identically at $3.79, but they are not identical in experience. The Caramel Sundae is the richest, sweetest, and highest-calorie of the three at 310 cal — 10 more than Hot Fudge and 30 more than Strawberry. Rich caramel sauce coats every spoonful of DQ soft serve with a buttery, sweet depth that chocolate and strawberry do not replicate. Find all dessert options on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Three DQ Sundaes Side by Side</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Sundae</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Flavor Profile</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Caramel Sundae</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>310</td><td>Buttery sweet caramel</td><td>Rich dessert fans</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/hot-fudge-sundae">Hot Fudge Sundae</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>300</td><td>Warm chocolate</td><td>Classic chocolate lovers</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/strawberry-sundae">Strawberry Sundae</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>280</td><td>Fruity strawberry</td><td>Lighter, fruit-forward</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>When to Order the Caramel Sundae</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>When you want maximum sweetness:</strong> Caramel is the sweetest of the three toppings. If you have a strong sweet tooth, caramel delivers more than fudge or strawberry.</li>
      <li><strong>After a salty meal:</strong> The salty-sweet contrast is one of the great food pairings. The Caramel Sundae after a <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc">Chicken Strip Basket</a> or <a href="/items/chili-cheese-dog">Chili Cheese Dog</a> works particularly well for this reason.</li>
      <li><strong>As a $7 Meal Deal dessert:</strong> The Caramel Sundae is eligible as the Small Sundae in the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> — the richest dessert you can get within that deal.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Caramel Sundae vs. Peanut Buster Parfait</h2>
    <p>If you love caramel, consider the <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a> ($4.99, 710 cal) — it replaces caramel with hot fudge and adds salted peanuts, but the layered parfait format delivers a more complex dessert experience. The Caramel Sundae at $3.79 is the simpler, lower-calorie, and lower-price option when you want something quick and satisfying.</p>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Eat immediately:</strong> Caramel sauce warms the soft serve faster than strawberry. The texture is best in the first two minutes.</li>
      <li><strong>Request extra caramel:</strong> Available at most locations for a small upcharge. Worthwhile if you want more sauce coverage.</li>
      <li><strong>Consider the Banana Split alternative:</strong> The <a href="/items/banana-split">Banana Split</a> ($5.69) includes caramel as one of its three toppings alongside pineapple and strawberry — a more complex option for $1.90 more.</li>
    </ul>

